// ProjectDeliveryS661 — Sprint 661: Close dcAdvanceRefusesAnyBoundStep (D0321 option A's second half): keel advance refuses --to any step whose earlier bound check is red, for ANY process, and the ceremony order it and three other readers enforce is read from the tree instead of a compiled table. Before this sprint the six-gate sequence lived in four places - orient.rs GATE_ORDER, guards.rs GATE_ORDER, algo.rs CEREMONY_GATES, and an include_str test holding one of them to delivery.sysml - and only the agile-workflow's steps had an in-loop refusal, hand-coded. After it: a ProcessStep may bind `gate:<phase>` (D0435, proposed), the six ceremony steps carry theirs through the D0434 transform's second run, orient::gate_order reads the workflow chain the bound phases belong to, and `keel advance <process> [--to <step>]` evaluates each step's guard or rule on the tree and refuses a forward move past a red one (D0436, proposed). The sprint also carries the finding made while recording its Decisions: check-engine passes a file keel check rejects (issue467).. EXECUTE. 5 pts.
